🎯 24 JavaScript Interview Q&A (2026 Market-Relevant)
Core Concepts
Difference between var, let, and const?  
var is function-scoped, let and const are block-scoped. const prevents reassignment. Modern JS avoids var.

What is a closure?  
A closure is a function that retains access to variables in its outer scope even after that scope has finished execution.

Explain the event loop.  
JS is single-threaded; the event loop manages async tasks. Microtasks (Promises) run before macrotasks (setTimeout).

What is prototypal inheritance?  
Objects inherit directly from other objects via the prototype chain, unlike classical inheritance.

Explain hoisting.  
Variable and function declarations are moved to the top of scope during compilation.

Difference between == and ===?  
== allows type coercion, === checks both value and type strictly.

Async & ES2020+
What is Promise.any()?  
Resolves with the first fulfilled promise; rejects only if all fail.

Explain async/await.  
Syntactic sugar over Promises, making async code look synchronous.

What is AbortController?  
API to cancel fetch or async tasks.

Difference between Promise.all vs Promise.allSettled?  
all fails if one rejects; allSettled waits for all to finish regardless of outcome.

What is structuredClone()?  
Deeply clones objects, including complex types like Map, Set, and File.

Explain nullish coalescing (??).  
Returns the right-hand operand only if the left-hand is null or undefined.

Performance & Patterns
What is debouncing?  
Delays function execution until after a pause in events (e.g., typing).

What is throttling?  
Ensures a function runs at fixed intervals, regardless of event frequency.

Explain memoization.  
Caching function results to avoid recomputation.

Difference between deep clone vs shallow clone?  
Shallow copies references; deep clone copies nested objects too.

DOM & Browser APIs
What is event delegation?  
Attaching a single event listener to a parent element to manage child events.

Explain shadow DOM.  
Encapsulation mechanism for web components, isolating styles and markup.

Difference between localStorage and sessionStorage?  
Both store key-value pairs; localStorage persists across sessions, sessionStorage clears on tab close.

What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous code in JS?  
Sync code blocks execution; async code allows non-blocking operations.

Modern JS & Security
What are private class fields?  
Declared with #, accessible only within the class.

Explain Object.groupBy().  
Groups array elements into an object based on a callback function.

What is XSS in JavaScript?  
Cross-Site Scripting: malicious scripts injected into web apps. Prevented via sanitization.

What is CSRF in JavaScript apps?  
Cross-Site Request Forgery: attacker tricks user into executing unwanted actions. Prevented via tokens.
